WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:06.041
Hello, I’m Sam, this is my channel, this
is that Wikipedia list, and this… is That

00:00:06.041 --> 00:00:18.220
Wikipedia List.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:19.220
You can’t copy money.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:24.199
I don’t mean it’s illegal, that’s obvious,
I mean that you physically cannot copy money

00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:25.869
on a photocopier.

00:00:25.869 --> 00:00:30.480
This is probably the only thing in the world
that your copier will just simply refuse to

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:31.480
copy.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:35.539
With pretty much any modern copier, an error
message will come up if you put a banknote

00:00:35.539 --> 00:00:38.039
or something resembling a banknote in the
scanner.

00:00:38.039 --> 00:00:41.590
I’d tell you to try it, but there are so
many laws surrounding currency that I’m

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:45.070
pretty sure I’d have the police kicking
down my door tomorrow if I did.

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:46.550
You can just take my word for it.

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:50.320
It’s pretty interesting how money is detected
by photocopiers.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:54.860
For almost any major currency, there’s one
symbol that tells machines that what they're

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:56.199
seeing is money.

00:00:56.199 --> 00:00:59.910
It’s called the EURion constellation and
it looks like this.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:03.989
It was first discovered on the 10 euro note
in this cluster of circles, but has since

00:01:03.989 --> 00:01:10.750
been found on the American dollar, the Swedish
krona, the UK pound, and pretty much every

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:12.799
other major currency.

00:01:12.799 --> 00:01:18.560
Most photocopiers will, if they see this pattern
of dots, stop printing in an attempt to stop

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:19.560
counterfeit.

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:21.430
At least, that’s how it used to be.

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:25.860
More recently, copiers have moved to a system
called the Counterfeit Deterrence System which

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:29.190
is incredibly secretive and effective.

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:32.980
Nobody is really sure how it works, and while
the Eurion constellation might be part of

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:37.340
it, these security measures make it even more
difficult to copy banknotes.

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:42.469
Adobe photoshop, like most photo editing softwares,
has the Counterfeit Deterrence System built

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:45.500
in which lets you see just how well it works.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:49.840
Photoshop can of course detect this image
of a 10 pound note since it’s Eurion constellations

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:54.420
are clearly visable, but then it can also
detect it if the area is blacked out.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:59.380
It can even figure out that this tiny almost
completely blacked out image is part of a

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:02.010
US $20 bill and refuse to edit it.

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:03.010
There’s almost no way to make counterfeiting
completely impossible, but the point of measures

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:04.010
against it is to make it so difficult that
the resources that would be used to counterfeit

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:05.010
money would be more expensive than the money
that could be made.

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:06.010
If it’s so difficult to make money that
it’s not profitable, nobody will do it.

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:07.159
There’s a ton of different laws relating
to the duplication and publication of visuals

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:08.440
of currency.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:12.700
The US has 32 pages of laws related to currency.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:17.290
Along with the obvious illegality of counterfeit,
it’s also illegal in the US to print or

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:22.730
publish any illustration of currency, postage
stamps, or revenue stamps of any nation in

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:27.430
the world unless, of course, it’s a stamp
made under the Migratory Bird Hunting Stamp

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:31.560
Act of 1934, and no, that’s not a joke.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:36.310
It’s also illegal to deface currency in
any way or to use the image of currency in

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:37.310
any advertisement.

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:42.790
It is, however, legal to show authentic banknotes
in videos and films.

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:47.050
For this reason, in most cases, the money
used in movies is real.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:53.379
To legally create prop money, the bill has
to be less than 75% or more than 150% of the

00:02:53.379 --> 00:02:59.160
size of authentic currency, one sided, and
must be destroyed immediately after use.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:02.620
Unless they want to do something that’s
illegal with money, like burn it or otherwise

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:06.989
deface it, filmmakers will often use real
money just for simplicity’s sake.

00:03:06.989 --> 00:03:11.330
Some prop manufacturers will create a stack
of blank green paper then top it with one

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:13.821
real bill to give the appearance of stacks
of currency.

00:03:13.821 --> 00:03:15.220
Also, one final law that you may not realize
related to currency is that private businesses

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:16.220
in the US have zero obligation to accept dollars
as payment.

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:17.220
Legally, they’re just as allowed to accept
galleons.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:18.220
In conclusion, don’t mess around with counterfeit.

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:20.290
It will almost never end well.

